+## Pipeline invocation
+
+One invocation, `write Medium article <topic/source/instructions>` or `/generate-article ...`, runs the sequence below and stops at STOP for Max's review. Nothing publishes, schedules, or touches Medium.
+
+Semantic work (research, claim map, angle, drafting, edits, title, images, repairs) is yours, run on Sonnet through the `claude -p` subscription, never an API key. The deterministic CLI owns stage state, hash-bound artifacts, caching, gates, metrics and verification. Do not hand-run its gates, edit its state files, or lower a gate to get a PASS. The evaluator modules (`scripts.fingerprint_eval`, `scripts.medium_review`, `scripts.publish_route`) are called by the CLI; never reimplement them.
+
+### Hierarchy
+
+factual > source/link > semantic > quality > voice > fingerprint. A higher level always wins: never trade a fact, a source, a link or a meaning for voice or fingerprint gain.
+
+### Hard rules
+
+- Never fabricate experience, quotes, sources, credentials, numbers or results. A real gap (no first-hand data, an unresolved claim, a thin angle) becomes an AUTHOR OPPORTUNITY in the artifacts, never invented text.
+- Never optimize against Medium's detectors or any third-party AI detector, and never conceal a required disclosure (AI assistance, sponsorship, affiliation). Fingerprint work uses our own metrics only.
+- Do not use presenter or video frames as images.
+
+### Where it runs
+
+Run from the merged checkout `/Users/maxsmacmini/Desktop/Projects/social-poster-fingerprint-eval` (it holds `scripts/write_pipeline`; not the old `social-poster-write-pipeline` worktree). Its evaluator tree must be committed: a dirty tree blocks the integrity gate. Git and gh commands on this Mac go through `ssh localhost '<cmd>'` (Desktop privacy blocks direct access to the shared `.git`).
+
+```bash
+cd /Users/maxsmacmini/Desktop/Projects/social-poster-fingerprint-eval
+WP="env HTTPS_PROXY= HTTP_PROXY= $HOME/.local/bin/uv run --python 3.12 --with markdown-it-py==4.2.0 python -m scripts.write_pipeline"
+# gateway-backed steps (claims gate, critic, review, integrity, fpverify): prefix with  doppler run -p api_keys -c dev --
+# on PyPI TLS errors add UV_OFFLINE=1 to the env
+$WP init --package <articles/slug>      # records the V6 framework path and hash; BLOCKED_FRAMEWORK if unreadable
+$WP status --package P [--json]         # all stages
+$WP next --package P                    # next stage to work on
+$WP begin <stage> --package P           # action skip (cached) or run, with input paths and the artifact spec
+$WP submit <stage> --package P --file F [--report R]
+$WP run review|critic|integrity|hash|package|stop --package P
+$WP antifp baseline|rank|finish --package P
+$WP antifp try --file F --signal S --package P
+$WP repair try --file F --package P
+$WP repair done --package P
+$WP finalize --package P                # integrity, hash, package, stop in order
+$WP revalidate --package P              # after Max edits FINAL.md
+$WP rebase --reason "<why>" --package P # author-approved edit only
+```
+
+`begin` output is authoritative for a stage's exact name, inputs and artifact spec. If the CLI names a stage differently from this file, follow the CLI.
+
+Long gate steps (claims gate, critic, review, integrity, fpverify) can exceed 10 minutes. If the runtime forbids foreground commands over 10 minutes, run them in the background, redirect output to a log in the package, and poll the log and `status`; never kill and rerun a gate that is still working, and never treat a timeout as a PASS.
+
+### Sequence
+
+Loop per stage: `begin`; on `skip` move on; on `run` do the work and `submit` (or run the CLI command). Exit 1 means the artifact was rejected: read `reasons`, fix, resubmit.
+
+1. Research and sources (`source`, `research`): ingest every input into `sources/` and the manifest, then research until material claims and consequential objections are supported.
+2. Evidence and claim map (`research`): one claim per row with status, inspected URL and passage; plus the research delta.
+3. Angle and originality (`angle`): the contribution test, "what does this add beyond a summary?". `summary_only` ends the run NOT_READY with author opportunities. Then `outline`.
+4. Author and fingerprint generation brief (`brief`): the CLI builds a brief from the author corpus and the evaluator's fingerprint (measured signals to avoid, structural norms to match). `begin brief`, read the brief file in full, and load it before drafting. Do not draft without it.
+5. Draft (`draft`) with fingerprint resistance built in, following the brief. Avoid repetitive syntax, uniform sentence and paragraph lengths, structural symmetry, templated intros and conclusions, excess three-item lists, formulaic transitions and signposting, generic explanation, restatement and low burstiness. Match the author corpus. Vary rhythm because the material calls for it, never to game a metric.
+6. Fact, source and link check (`validate`).
+7. Editorial improvement (`editorial`).
+8. Author-voice check (`voice`).
+9. Fingerprint measurement and targeted repair (`antifp`): `baseline`, read the strongest signals, propose one local edit, `try`, repeat, `finish`.
+10. Fact, source, link and semantic recheck: the CLI reruns the claims and links gate on the post-fingerprint text. Any failure goes upstream (validate), not around.
+11. Medium editorial review (`review`, `run review`).
+12. Title and subtitle (`title`).
+13. Images, captions, ALT, provenance (`images`): high quality, no presenter or video frames.
+14. Independent final critic (`critic`, `run critic`): a separate `claude -p` process.
+15. Safe repair (`repair`): `repair try` per major finding, then `repair done`. A repair may add a supported sentence (see below).
+16. A fresh critic if the content changed since the last critic pass.
+17. Final fingerprint verification (`fpverify`): baseline versus final on our own metrics.
+18. Final claim, link, source and structure integrity gate (`integrity`): the exact bytes of `FINAL.md`; always reruns, never cached.
+19. Exact final hash (`hash`).
+20. Package (`package`, `finalize` runs 18 to 21 in order).
+21. STOP (`stop`): state READY_FOR_REVIEW or NOT_READY. Report the package path, final hash, route recommendation, remaining fingerprint signals and author opportunities, then wait for Max.
+
+### Submit schemas
+
+Every submitted file must be UTF-8 and inside the package. JSON stages take a JSON object; text stages take Markdown, with `--report` JSON where stated.
+
+- `research` JSON: `claims[]` each with `id`, `claim`, `status` (`supported`, `attributed`, `inferred`, `unresolved`, as the CLI spec lists), and `evidence[]` with `url` (or `source_id`) plus `passage` actually inspected. A `supported` or `attributed` claim with no inspected url/source_id and passage is rejected.
+- `validate` needs `--report`, the factual report:
+
+```json
+{"checked": [{"claim_id": "c1", "verdict": "supported"}, {"claim_id": "c7", "verdict": "omitted"}],
+ "removals": [{"text": "<exact sentence removed>", "reason": "unresolved c7"}]}
+```
+
+  `checked[].claim_id` must be a string; every research claim id appears exactly once, none unknown, none duplicated. Every claim whose research status is `unresolved` must have verdict `omitted` (or `removed`) and must not be asserted in the text in any wording, verbatim or paraphrased; a semantic check catches paraphrase.
+- `editorial` and `voice` `--report` must attest the unslop gate: `{"unslop": {"applied": true, "prose_checker": "ran"}}` (`"unavailable"` is allowed only if disclosed). Both may add `removals`: `[{"text": "<exact reference sentence>", "reason": "..."}]`. A removal counts only if the sentence matches a reference sentence exactly (inline markup and whitespace ignored) and is really gone; undeclared deletions, changed claims and added claims block.
+- `antifp`: local edits only. A `try` changes at most 3 blocks, and is kept only if the targeted `--signal` (one of `template_hits`, `em_dash_per_1k`, `repeated_ngram`, `one_sentence_para_excess`, `transition_excess`) improves, the composite improves by more than 0.05, the edit guard holds (no link or number lost or invented, headings, code, images and frozen blocks unchanged, no invented experience) and the claims gate passes. At most 12 attempts. The text is NOT_READY as fingerprint-heavy if `template_hits` is 4 or more, or the composite is 18.0 or more, after `finish`. Do not edit `current.md` by hand; only gated `try` output is accepted.
+- `title` JSON: at least 10 `candidates`, one `pick` from them, `rationale`, `subtitle` of at most 140 characters. No em dash, corrective contrast, clickbait or reveal-question in the title or subtitle.
+- `images` JSON: per image `id`, `path` (inside the package), `purpose`, `placement` (`hero`, `after:<heading>` or `after-paragraph:<n>`), `method`, `provenance`, `license`, `caption`, `alt` (10 to 220 characters); a `sourced` image needs `source_url`. Hero at least 1200x600. Or `waived_reason` with an empty list.
+- `repair try --file`: a full revised candidate. It must pass the edit guard and the claims gate against the reference. A repair may add a sentence only if that sentence is supported: it restates a `supported` or `attributed` research claim with an inspected passage already in the evidence map, adds no new number or link, and carries no invented experience; the CLI rejects an added sentence it cannot trace to the evidence ledger. A fix that needs a new or changed claim is rejected; after 3 rejections the run is NOT_READY. Rework upstream instead.
+
+### Budgets and exits
+
+- The critic budget is 3 per run and does not reset, not after a repair, a rebase, a revalidate or an upstream rework. Once spent with a major finding open, the run is NOT_READY.
+- The upstream-rework limit is 1 per stage. Going back to a stage to fix a downstream finding is allowed once for that stage; a second rework of the same stage ends the run NOT_READY.
+- Exit codes: 3 NOT_READY, 4 BLOCKED (model or evaluator unavailable: report it and retry later, never self-grade instead), 5 QUARANTINED, 6 FINAL.md changed after PASS. On 3 and 5 stop and report the exact reasons; do not route around them. Exit 2 means an upstream stage is missing.
+- `rebase` exists only for an author-approved edit. It reruns the claims and links gate against the previous reference, is refused when that gate fails, and never marks the final gate PASS.
+- If READY is not reachable, produce NOT_READY honestly: the package with the remaining findings, no softened gate.
+
+When Max edits `FINAL.md` after the PASS, the CLI detects the hash change on the next command and refuses to proceed until `revalidate` reruns the critic and the final gate and repackages.
+
+### PACKAGE.md sections
+
+In this order, all required: TITLE, SUBTITLE, ARTICLE, SOURCES, IMAGES, EDITORIAL SCORECARD, AUTHOR-VOICE RESULT, FINGERPRINT BASELINE, FINGERPRINT FINAL, FINGERPRINT CHANGES, REMAINING FINGERPRINT SIGNALS, CLAIM CHECK, LINK CHECK, SOURCE CHECK, STRUCTURE CHECK, SEMANTIC PRESERVATION, MEDIUM REVIEW, EXACT FINAL HASH, READY/NOT_READY. Author opportunities and the Medium route recommendation (never an action) are reported with them.
+
